# Tutorials. Each story is one tutorial in the docs and one acceptance test: its
# introduction is the text under the narrative, and each When is a numbered step.

Story: Your first throw
  As a new pilot
  I want to throw the plane by opening the throttle, like at the field
  So that launching in the sim feels like the real thing

  You launch the T1-S by hand. At the field, you hold it up, open the throttle and let it
  go. The sim works in the same way. In this tutorial, you throw the plane one time. Then
  you bring it back to your hand, so that you can throw it again.

  Scenario: Throttle up, then pick it back up
    When the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Then the plane is flying
    When the pilot closes the throttle
    Then the throttle is 0 %
    When the pilot resets the plane
    Then the plane is in hand

Story: Watching from every view
  As a pilot
  I want to see the plane from the pilot box, from behind it and from its nose camera
  So that I can fly the way I like and watch it the way I want

  You can see the plane in three views. [[Line of sight]] is from the pilot box, as you fly
  at the field. [[Chase]] is from behind the plane, and [[FPV]] is through its nose camera.
  Throw the plane, then look at it in each view.

  Scenario: Throw it, then step through the views
    When the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Then the plane is flying
    When the pilot changes the view
    Then the view is chase
    When the pilot changes the view
    Then the view is FPV
    When the pilot changes the view
    Then the view is line of sight

Story: Learning with self-levelling
  As a pilot learning to fly
  I want the plane to level itself when I let go of the sticks
  So that I can learn the controls without it getting away from me

  In [[ANGLE]], the plane levels its wings when you release the sticks. Thus the plane stays
  under control while you learn. In this tutorial, you select ANGLE, throw the plane and roll
  it. Then you release the stick, and the wings become level again.

  Scenario: Pick ANGLE mode and throw
    When the pilot changes flight mode
    Then the flight mode is ANGLE
    When the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Then the plane is flying
    When the pilot rolls the plane to the left
    Then the wings are banked
    When the pilot releases the roll stick
    Then the wings are level
    When the pilot closes the throttle
    Then the throttle is 0 %
    When the pilot resets the plane
    Then the plane is in hand

Story: Crashing and starting again
  As a pilot
  I want to pick the plane up again straight after a crash
  So that a mistake costs seconds, not a repair

  A crash in the sim costs nothing. In this tutorial, you throw the plane with the nose
  down, so that it crashes. Then you pick it up again.

  Scenario: Nose it in, then reset
    When the pilot throws the plane nose-down
    Then the plane is crashed
    When the pilot lets go and closes the throttle
    Then the throttle is 0 %
    When the pilot resets the plane
    Then the plane is in hand

Story: Taking a break
  As a pilot
  I want to stop time mid-flight
  So that I can look around or read the help without losing the plane

  You can stop time during a flight. Then you can look around, read the help or rest. The
  plane stays where it is until you continue.

  Scenario: Pause, read the help, carry on
    When the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Then the plane is flying
    When the pilot toggles pause
    Then the sim is paused
    When the pilot toggles the help
    Then the help screen is shown
    When the pilot closes the help
    Then the help screen is hidden
    When the pilot toggles pause
    Then the sim is running

Story: Checking the controls before a flight
  As a new pilot
  I want to look up the keys before I throw
  So that I know how to fly before the plane is in the air

  The help screen shows all the keys and what they do. Open it before your first throw. Open
  it again when you forget a key.

  Scenario: Open the help and close it again
    When the pilot toggles the help
    Then the help screen is shown
    When the pilot toggles the help
    Then the help screen is hidden
